# Week 6 - Spark Intro

This repository contains my Week 6 PySpark practical implementation. It demonstrates how to read, transform, filter, and save data using Apache Spark DataFrames.

## Topics Covered

- Reading CSV and Parquet files
- DataFrame operations
- Selecting and filtering data
- Renaming columns
- Data type conversion
- Creating new columns
- Handling null values
- Aggregations (GroupBy)
- Predicate Pushdown
- Building ETL/Data Pipelines
- Saving data as CSV and Parquet

## Technologies Used

- Python
- PySpark
- Apache Spark
- Jupyter Notebook

##  Workflow

Read Data
   ↓
Transform Data
   ↓
Filter Records
   ↓
Handle Null Values
   ↓
Aggregate Data
   ↓
Write Output (CSV/Parquet)

## Learning Outcomes

- Learned Spark DataFrame operations
- Built an end-to-end ETL pipeline
- Worked with CSV and Parquet formats
- Performed data cleaning and transformations
- Saved processed data efficiently
